 "utterances": [
  {
   "start": 2.38,
   "end": 6.58,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Morning, everyone. Bit of a short week, then. Can everyone hear me?"
  },
  {
   "start": 7.63,
   "end": 10.78,
   "speaker_id": "p04",
   "speaker": "Tomasz Nowak",
   "text": "Yeah, but there's two of you. One's quite enough."
  },
  {
   "start": 11.96,
   "end": 15.11,
   "speaker_id": "p08",
   "speaker": "Marcus Hale",
   "text": "That's my end, sorry. Teams and the laptop speaker."
  },
  {
   "start": 16.03,
   "end": 17.78,
   "speaker_id": "p08",
   "speaker": "Marcus Hale",
   "text": "There. Headset's actually connected now."
  },
  {
   "start": 18.36,
   "end": 22.21,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Lovely. Jamie Brennan's absent today. Otherwise I think we're all here."
  },
  {
   "start": 22.55,
   "end": 25.35,
   "speaker_id": "p06",
   "speaker": "Callum Reid",
   "text": "Yep, I'm here. Camera's off, but I'm here."
  },
  {
   "start": 26.71,
   "end": 31.26,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Right, updates first, then a few new bits. How are you getting on?"
  },
  {
   "start": 31.88,
   "end": 38.18,
   "speaker_id": "p06",
   "speaker": "Callum Reid",
   "text": "Yeah so, booking the contractor for the Arburg — done the prep, just the write-up left on that."
  },
  {
   "start": 39.02,
   "end": 40.22,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Okay, cheers."
  },
  {
   "start": 42.71,
   "end": 50.76,
   "speaker_id": "p06",
   "speaker": "Callum Reid",
   "text": "And the risk assessment for work, I've got the prep done there as well. Just the write-up left. Bit of a theme, unfortunately."
  },
  {
   "start": 51.61,
   "end": 54.06,
   "speaker_id": "p09",
   "speaker": "Fiona Doyle",
   "text": "The paperwork always outlasts the interesting bit."
  },
  {
   "start": 55.31,
   "end": 56.71,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Doesn't it just. Tommo?"
  },
  {
   "start": 59.17,
   "end": 64.42,
   "speaker_id": "p04",
   "speaker": "Tomasz Nowak",
   "text": "I've made a start on checking the guarding on the stacker. Only partway through it."
  },
  {
   "start": 65.88,
   "end": 70.43,
   "speaker_id": "p04",
   "speaker": "Tomasz Nowak",
   "text": "And that filter swap, I've had a first look. Nothing major so far."
  },
  {
   "start": 71.43,
   "end": 72.63,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Right, thanks. Olumide?"
  },
  {
   "start": 73.73,
   "end": 76.53,
   "speaker_id": "p10",
   "speaker": "Olumide Adeyemi",
   "text": "Monthly fire alarm test's all done. All fine."
  },
  {
   "start": 77.65,
   "end": 80.1,
   "speaker_id": "p06",
   "speaker": "Callum Reid",
   "text": "Nice. That's what you want to hear."
  },
  {
   "start": 81.42,
   "end": 91.22,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Also, Haley asked me to pass on that the new starters' training records need to come off his list. Olumide, I'm moving those over to you to sort."
  },
  {
   "start": 93.41,
   "end": 97.61,
   "speaker_id": "p10",
   "speaker": "Olumide Adeyemi",
   "text": "Yeah, I'll take over sorting the training records for the new starters."
  },
  {
   "start": 98.13,
   "end": 99.53,
   "speaker_id": "p08",
   "speaker": "Marcus Hale",
   "text": "Thanks, mate. Appreciate that."
  },
  {
   "start": 100.97,
   "end": 103.07,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Okay. New bits for today, then."
  },
  {
   "start": 105.03,
   "end": 110.28,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Aisha Begum, can you order spare parts for the outfeed conveyor on Friday? Normal priority."
  },
  {
   "start": 110.75,
   "end": 115.65,
   "speaker_id": "p07",
   "speaker": "Aisha Begum",
   "text": "Yeah, just checking — order placed on Friday, not parts landed here on Friday?"
  },
  {
   "start": 118.02,
   "end": 120.82,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "That's right, order placed. Not a delivery deadline."
  },
  {
   "start": 121.97,
   "end": 127.57,
   "speaker_id": "p07",
   "speaker": "Aisha Begum",
   "text": "Fine, I'll order the spare parts for the outfeed conveyor on Friday. Normal priority, got it."
  },
  {
   "start": 128.12,
   "end": 132.32,
   "speaker_id": "p09",
   "speaker": "Fiona Doyle",
   "text": "Yeah, makes sense. Order date and delivery date get muddled so easily."
  },
  {
   "start": 132.97,
   "end": 139.27,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Marc, can you chase the purchase order for the Boiler Feedwater Pump this morning? That one's fairly important."
  },
  {
   "start": 140.8,
   "end": 144.65,
   "speaker_id": "p08",
   "speaker": "Marcus Hale",
   "text": "Yeah, so chasing the PO, rather than putting another order in."
  },
  {
   "start": 147.02,
   "end": 148.42,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Exactly. Just the chase."
  },
  {
   "start": 149.25,
   "end": 154.85,
   "speaker_id": "p08",
   "speaker": "Marcus Hale",
   "text": "Yep, I'll chase the purchase order for the Boiler Feedwater Pump this morning. Understood, fairly important."
  },
  {
   "start": 156.09,
   "end": 158.19,
   "speaker_id": "p04",
   "speaker": "Tomasz Nowak",
   "text": "The glamorous side of engineering, that."
  },
  {
   "start": 160.65,
   "end": 163.8,
   "speaker_id": "p08",
   "speaker": "Marcus Hale",
   "text": "Oh, living the dream. Headset on, purchase order numbers."
  },
  {
   "start": 166.29,
   "end": 172.59,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Fiona Doyle, can you write up the near miss at the pick and place on two after lunch?"
  },
  {
   "start": 174.37,
   "end": 177.17,
   "speaker_id": "p09",
   "speaker": "Fiona Doyle",
   "text": "Sorry, you clipped a bit there. After lunch?"
  },
  {
   "start": 179.05,
   "end": 180.25,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Yes, after lunch."
  },
  {
   "start": 182.71,
   "end": 188.66,
   "speaker_id": "p09",
   "speaker": "Fiona Doyle",
   "text": "Right, yes. I'll write up the near miss at the pick and place on two after lunch."
  },
  {
   "start": 191.13,
   "end": 195.68,
   "speaker_id": "p06",
   "speaker": "Callum Reid",
   "text": "You're clear again now, Sarah. It went a bit robotic for a second."
  },
  {
   "start": 196.44,
   "end": 204.84,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Good old Teams. Haley, one more for you: can you check the guarding on the door switch on two next Tuesday? Top priority please."
  },
  {
   "start": 206.04,
   "end": 208.14,
   "speaker_id": "p08",
   "speaker": "Marcus Hale",
   "text": "Next Tuesday, yeah? Not this Tuesday?"
  },
  {
   "start": 209.25,
   "end": 212.4,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Next Tuesday, yes. Top priority please for that check."
  },
  {
   "start": 213.94,
   "end": 219.54,
   "speaker_id": "p08",
   "speaker": "Marcus Hale",
   "text": "Okay, I'll check the guarding on the door switch on two next Tuesday. Got the priority."
  },
  {
   "start": 220.43,
   "end": 223.58,
   "speaker_id": "p07",
   "speaker": "Aisha Begum",
   "text": "Bank holiday's thrown my sense of the week completely."
  },
  {
   "start": 223.92,
   "end": 228.12,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Same here. Right, that's the work covered. Anything else before we finish?"
  },
  {
   "start": 229.91,
   "end": 237.26,
   "speaker_id": "p04",
   "speaker": "Tomasz Nowak",
   "text": "Only that the charity bake sale on Friday is apparently very competitive this year. Not a work item, just slightly alarming."
  },
  {
   "start": 239.72,
   "end": 242.17,
   "speaker_id": "p09",
   "speaker": "Fiona Doyle",
   "text": "Competitive how? Are people measuring the cakes?"
  },
  {
   "start": 244.18,
   "end": 247.33,
   "speaker_id": "p04",
   "speaker": "Tomasz Nowak",
   "text": "Wouldn't surprise me. Mine would fail the visual inspection."
  },
  {
   "start": 249.05,
   "end": 251.5,
   "speaker_id": "p06",
   "speaker": "Callum Reid",
   "text": "Never mind visual. What's the hardness reading?"
  },
  {
   "start": 253.03,
   "end": 259.33,
   "speaker_id": "p10",
   "speaker": "Olumide Adeyemi",
   "text": "Sorry, talking over you — I was going to say, depends whether it's cake or a test piece."
  },
  {
   "start": 260.56,
   "end": 261.96,
   "speaker_id": "p08",
   "speaker": "Marcus Hale",
   "text": "With his baking, both."
  },
  {
   "start": 262.75,
   "end": 265.55,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Right, before this turns into a materials review..."
  },
  {
   "start": 266.84,
   "end": 270.34,
   "speaker_id": "p07",
   "speaker": "Aisha Begum",
   "text": "Strong start to a Tuesday. We've already got cake tolerances."
  },
  {
   "start": 271.74,
   "end": 273.49,
   "speaker_id": "p04",
   "speaker": "Tomasz Nowak",
   "text": "Cruel, this team. Absolutely cruel."
  },
  {
   "start": 275.1,
   "end": 278.6,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "And on that note, thanks everyone. We'll leave it there."
  },
  {
   "start": 279.65,
   "end": 280.85,
   "speaker_id": "p09",
   "speaker": "Fiona Doyle",
   "text": "Cheers, all."
  },
  {
   "start": 282.76,
   "end": 283.96,
   "speaker_id": "p08",
   "speaker": "Marcus Hale",
   "text": "Cheers."
  },
  {
   "start": 285.28,
   "end": 286.48,
   "speaker_id": "p10",
   "speaker": "Olumide Adeyemi",
   "text": "Thanks, bye."
  }
 ],
